# AI PDF Accessibility Remediation for Plone

The **AI PDF Accessibility Remediation Add-on** brings **PDF Accessibility Remediation for WCAG & PDF/UA Compliance** directly into your own Plone site. It is both a **PDF Accessibility Checker** and an **AI Remediation Tool**: upload documents or crawl your website for them, let AI repair the accessibility barriers automatically, review every check that was applied, and download conformant files — without leaving Plone.

It fixes the barriers that make PDFs unusable with assistive technology: missing tags, incorrect reading order, inaccessible forms and tables, images without alternate text, and absent document structure, language and metadata.

It supports compliance with **WCAG 2.0, 2.1, 2.2, PDF/UA, ADA, Section 508, AODA, and EN 301 549 (EAA)**. With plain-language explanations and before/after examples for every check, even non-technical users can understand what was fixed and why it mattered.

This build is a **Plone add-on** (`plone-SkynetA11y-pdf-remediation`, v1.0.0) — a normal pip-installable package with no extra bundler or build step. It installs from **Site Setup → Add-ons** like any other Plone product, works on **Plone 6.0, 6.1 and 6.2**, and adds the dashboard to your site's own administration area.

This add-on is designed for:

- Businesses of all sizes
- Enterprises
- Government and public sector entities
- Website owners
- E-commerce platforms
- Development and maintenance agencies

[**Start with a free AI remediation trial — up to 5 pages!**](https://www.skynettechnologies.com/pdf-accessibility-remediation)

---

## Why AI PDF Accessibility Remediation?

PDFs are where accessibility compliance quietly fails. A site can pass every page-level audit and still publish hundreds of untagged documents — reports, forms, invoices, policies — that screen readers cannot navigate at all.

Remediating them by hand is slow and expensive. This add-on makes it a routine part of publishing: documents are discovered, repaired and re-checked inside the tools your team already uses, so accessible PDFs become the default rather than a project.

## Key Features

- **SkynetA11y PDF Remediation** – Automated repair of tags, reading order, alt text, headings, tables and metadata.
- **PDF Accessibility Checker** – Every check reported individually, expandable to a plain-language explanation and a before/after example.
- **Upload or Crawl** – Add files by drag and drop, or sweep your website for every PDF it links to.
- **Free Trial** – The free plan covers your first 5 pages; paid plans scale from 50 to 10,000 pages.
- **Bulk Remediation** – Select any number of documents and process them in one run, with live progress.
- **Deep Tag Scan** – Post-remediation verification against the document's tag tree, not just its declared metadata.
- **Authenticated Downloads** – Remediated files are delivered over an authenticated session, never a public link.
- **No Settings Screen Required** – Nothing to paste and nothing to wire up out of the box. One short dialog asks for a name, email and domain the first time it is needed, and never again — or an administrator can pin these in the Plone configuration registry ahead of time (see [Configuration](#configuration)).
- **Built into Plone** – A **Site Setup → SkynetA11y PDF Remediation Dashboard** entry (with a "Back to Plone" button on the standalone page), restricted to Managers and Site Administrators.
- **Integration with All in One Accessibility® Dashboard** – Plans, usage and billing stay in one place.

## Compliance Standards Supported

- WCAG 2.0, 2.1, 2.2
- PDF/UA (ISO 14289)
- ADA
- Section 508
- AODA
- EN 301 549 (EU / European Accessibility Act)

## Compatibility

| Plone | Python | Status |
|---|---|---|
| **6.2** (latest, 6.2.2) | 3.10 – 3.14 | Tested on 3.10, 3.12 and 3.14 |
| **6.1** | 3.10 – 3.13 | Tested on 6.1.5 / Python 3.13 |
| **6.0** | 3.10 – 3.11 | Tested on 6.0.0 / Python 3.10 |
| 5.2 and earlier | – | Not supported (end of life) |

The add-on uses the Classic UI (server-rendered) and works on any Plone 6 site that has it. On a Volto site, the dashboard is served by the Plone backend at `<backend-url>/@@pdf-remediation-dashboard`.

## Installation

1. **Install the package** into the same Python environment as Plone:
   ```
   pip install plone-SkynetA11y-pdf-remediation
   ```
   ```
   or, with buildout:
   ```ini
   [instance]
   eggs +=
       plone-SkynetA11y-pdf-remediation
   ```
   Plone loads the add-on's configuration automatically. (On a very old buildout that does not autoinclude, also add `zcml += plone_SkynetA11y_pdf_remediation`.)
2. **Restart Plone**, e.g. `./bin/instance restart` (or however your environment restarts — systemd, Docker, supervisord, etc.).
3. Go to **Site Setup → Add-ons** and click **Install** next to **SkynetA11y PDF Remediation**.
4. Open **Site Setup → Add-on Configuration → SkynetA11y PDF Remediation Dashboard**, or go straight to
   **`<your-site>/@@pdf-remediation-dashboard`**.

That is all: no database migration and nothing to configure.

### Upgrading

Install the new version, restart Plone, then open **Site Setup → Add-ons** and click **Upgrade** next to SkynetA11y PDF Remediation if it is offered. Upgrades never overwrite values you have set, and static files are versioned, so browsers pick up the new JavaScript and CSS without a manual cache clear.

Coming from an earlier build that had an *SkynetA11y PDF Remediation Settings* page? Running the upgrade removes that entry; the dashboard is now the only screen.

### Uninstalling

Use **Site Setup → Add-ons → Uninstall**. This removes the Site Setup entry and the stored settings. Your PDFs and remediated files live in the remediation service, not in Plone, and are not affected.

## How It Works

1. **Add Your PDFs** – Upload files, or crawl your website for every PDF it links to.
2. **Run AI Remediation** – Select documents and process them in bulk; progress is reported live.
3. **Review & Download** – Inspect each accessibility check with its explanation and before/after example, then download the conformant file.

